== Implemented exact instrument

The native core:

- validates canonical IR and a nonempty proper vertex side;
- leaves canonical cut edges open and rejects cut pins;
- enumerates all admitted free internal assignments under an explicit cap;
- evaluates the digest-bound truth table or typed program at every selected predicate;
- emits exact arbitrary-precision boundary counts, support and a stable tensor digest;
- computes canonical and exhaustive balanced ranks with fraction-free integer elimination; and
- records big-integer operation counts and strict JSON provenance.

Development checks pass for ranks 1, 2 and 4; a canonical equality network; cap and pin failures; and 1,152 deterministic matrices cross-checked against rational Gaussian elimination. Rust 1.78 focused release tests and CLI build pass. Current-stable all-target Clippy passes with warnings denied.

